sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client
    participant M as loginRequired middleware
    participant AS as AuthService
    participant UR as UserRepository
    participant Ctrl as Controller
    participant Svc as Service

    C->>M: request with Authorization: Bearer <token>
    M->>AS: authenticate(authorizationHeader)

    alt no Authorization header
        AS-->>M: throws UnauthorizedError('Login required')
    else header present
        AS->>AS: jwt.verify(token, TOKEN_SECRET)
        alt token invalid or expired
            AS-->>M: throws UnauthorizedError('Expired or invalid token.')
        else token valid
            AS->>UR: findByIdAndEmail(id, email)
            UR-->>AS: User | null
            alt user no longer exists
                AS-->>M: throws UnauthorizedError('Invalid User')
            else user exists
                AS-->>M: { userId, userEmail }
                M->>M: req.userId = userId
                M->>Ctrl: next()
                Ctrl->>Svc: business logic call
                Svc-->>Ctrl: result
                Ctrl-->>C: 200 response
            end
        end
    end

    Note over M,C: Any thrown UnauthorizedError propagates to errorHandler,<br/>which responds 401 { errors: [...] }.
